{"name":"Boudoir Beige","hex":"#d9c0ab","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"boudoir","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A woman's private sitting room, dressing room, or bedroom.","An army tent."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/boudoir"},{"term":"beige","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A colour, variously defined from a pale brown, to a yellow greyish off-white.","Debeige; a kind of woollen or mixed dress goods."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a slightly yellowish gray colour, as that of unbleached wool.","Comfortably dull and unadventurous, in a way that suggests middle-class suburbia."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beige"}],"entries":[{"title":"Boudoir","blocks":[{"text":"A boudoir is a lady’s private sitting room or salon in a furnished residence, usually between the dining room and the bedroom, but can also refer to a lady’s private bedroom. The term derives from the French verb bouder or adjective boudeur (sulking)—the room was originally a space to withdraw to."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Poland_Niebor%C3%B3w_Palace_008.jpg/330px-Poland_Niebor%C3%B3w_Palace_008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Boudoir","wikidata":"Q62238"},{"title":"Beige","blocks":[{"text":"Beige is variously described as a pale sandy fawn color, a grayish tan, a light-grayish yellowish brown, or a pale to grayish yellow. It takes its name from French, where the word originally meant natural wool that has been neither bleached nor dyed, hence also the color of natural wool."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a5/Saint_Anthony_church_in_Chamboret_07.jpg/330px-Saint_Anthony_church_in_Chamboret_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beige","wikidata":"Q843607"}],"images":[{"srcset":